{#
sharing/shared_calendar.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Somebody's calendar, as much of it as their link reveals — drawn as a calendar.

**This template cannot leak, and the reason is what it is given.** `month.days`
and `view.days` hold SharedOccurrence objects, not events: on a busy/free link
their `title`, `location` and `description` are already null and `participants`
is already empty, decided once in ShareLinkReader against the link's checkboxes
AND the event's own privacy. So there is no `if` here that could be forgotten,
no tooltip that could carry a subject, and no data attribute that could carry
one into JavaScript. Adding a field to this page means adding it to the DTO
first, which is where the decision about revealing it has to be made.

The month grid is a rearrangement of exactly those objects and nothing else —
see SharedCalendarMonthBuilder, which has no repository and could not fetch more
if it wanted to.

The counterpart rule: nothing below may reach for `app.user`, a session, or a
CSRF token. See sharing/_layout.html.twig for why.

── A grid AND a list, which is a change of mind, recorded ──────────────────

This page used to be a list of days and nothing else, on the argument that a
grid needs a viewport, a scroll position and a zone control to be readable and
that this page is opened once, usually on a phone, by somebody who was asked to
look at it. That argument was right about phones and wrong about everything
else: a calendar that arrives as a list does not look like a calendar, which is
not what the person who sent the link thought they were sending.

So both, from the same objects. The grid is the app's own month — literally, via
calendar/_month_shell.html.twig — and carries a mark per entry. The list under
it carries the detail, is the only thing worth reading on a narrow screen, and
keeps the property the old page was built around: every shared day in the month
is printed, including the empty ones, so "free on the 4th" is a thing the page
says rather than a gap the reader has to notice.

── Days outside the window are not free days ───────────────────────────────

A month has 42 cells; a rolling link publishes fourteen days. The cells the link
does not cover are drawn dimmed, absent from the list, and named in a legend,
because a blank cell that looked like a free one would make this page claim
something about its owner's diary that its owner never published. Paging is
bounded to the months the window actually touches for the same reason.

Variables:
  view            SharedCalendarView   window, zone, and days keyed Y-m-d
  month           SharedCalendarMonth  those days as a 42-cell grid, plus the steps
  token           string               this link's own URL segment, for the paging
  icsPath         string               where the same window is downloadable
  appearance      PublicAppearance     the owner's theme
  chipTimeFormat  string               a PHP date() format for a grid cell: compact
  rowTimeFormat   string               the same clock, spelled in full, for the list
#}
{% extends 'sharing/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block container_class %}max-w-3xl{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <header class="mb-4">
        <h1 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{{ 'calendar.share.heading'|trans }}</h1>

        {# `window_label`, not `window`. The latter is a two-child node —
           `window.fixed` and `window.rolling`, which the settings form uses for
           its radio labels — and asking the translator for the parent got the
           key itself printed on the page under the heading. It has said
           "calendar.share.window" to every recipient since the feature shipped;
           `bin/console debug:translation en --only-missing` lists it, which is
           where it was finally caught. #}
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-muted">
            {{ 'calendar.share.window_label'|trans({
                '%from%': view.from|date('j M Y'),
                '%to%': view.to|date_modify('-1 day')|date('j M Y'),
            }) }}
        </p>

        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            {# Named on every page, not only when it differs from the reader's. The
               reader has no account here, so there is no stored preference to
               compare against, and a list of hours with no zone beside it is the
               single most reliable way to make somebody miss a meeting. #}
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-sunken px-2.5 py-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-clock text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ 'calendar.share.zone'|trans({ '%zone%': view.zone }) }}
            </span>

            {% if view.isBusyFreeOnly %}
                <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-sunken px-2.5 py-1 text-xs text-ink-muted">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-eye-slash text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    {{ 'calendar.share.busy_free_only'|trans }}
                </span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden bg-surface">
        {# The toolbar of a read-only calendar: where you are, and the two ways
           out of it. No view switcher — a link publishes one window and there is
           no second arrangement of it to offer — and no "today", which would be
           a control that does nothing whenever the window does not contain it.
           A step that leaves the window is rendered as a disabled span rather
           than omitted, so the row does not change shape as you page. #}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 border-b border-line min-h-[var(--pane-header-h)]">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-0.5 shrink-0">
                {% if month.previous is not null %}
                    <a href="{{ path('app_shared_calendar_show', { token: token, month: month.previous }) }}"
                       class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors"
                       aria-label="{{ 'calendar.nav.previous'|trans }}"
                    ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-faint opacity-40"
                          aria-hidden="true"
                    ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left text-xs"></i></span>
                {% endif %}

                {% if month.next is not null %}
                    <a href="{{ path('app_shared_calendar_show', { token: token, month: month.next }) }}"
                       class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-muted hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors"
                       aria-label="{{ 'calendar.nav.next'|trans }}"
                    ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                {% else %}
                    <span class="w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-ink-faint opacity-40"
                          aria-hidden="true"
                    ><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right text-xs"></i></span>
                {% endif %}
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink truncate min-w-0">{{ month.anchor|date('F Y') }}</h2>
        </div>

        {# `auto-rows` rather than the authenticated calendar's `h-full`: that
           grid lives in a pane with a height of its own to divide up, and this
           one is in a document that is as tall as it needs to be. A minimum per
           row is what stops a quiet month collapsing into six thin stripes. #}
        {% embed 'calendar/_month_shell.html.twig' with {
            dayKeys: month.dayKeys,
            days: month.gridDays,
            anchorMonth: month.anchor|date('n'),
            today: 'now'|date('Y-m-d', view.zone),
            shellOuterClass: 'flex flex-col',
            shellRowsClass: 'auto-rows-[minmax(3.25rem,auto)] sm:auto-rows-[minmax(5.5rem,auto)]',
        } %}
            {% block cell_body %}
                <div class="min-h-0 flex-1 space-y-0.5 overflow-hidden">
                    {% for entry in dayEntries|slice(0, 3) %}
                        {% include 'sharing/_entry_chip.html.twig' with {
                            entry: entry,
                            zone: view.zone,
                            timeFormat: chipTimeFormat,
                        } only %}
                    {% endfor %}

                    {% if dayEntries|length > 3 %}
                        <p class="px-0.5 sm:px-1.5 text-[10px] sm:text-[11px] text-ink-faint">
                            {{ 'calendar.more_count'|trans({ '%count%': dayEntries|length - 3 }) }}
                        </p>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            {% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}
    </section>

    <p class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[11px] text-ink-faint">
        <span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 rounded-sm bg-sunken/20 border border-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {{ 'calendar.share.outside_window'|trans }}
    </p>

    {% if view.isEmpty %}
        <p class="mt-6 rounded-pane border border-line px-4 py-10 text-center text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
            {{ 'calendar.share.empty'|trans }}
        </p>
    {% else %}
        <ol class="mt-6 space-y-4">
            {% for day in month.sharedDays %}
                <li class="rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden bg-surface">
                    <h3 class="px-4 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-ink-soft bg-sunken border-b border-line">
                        {{ day.date|date('l, j F Y') }}
                    </h3>

                    {% if day.entries is empty %}
                        <p class="px-4 py-3 text-sm text-ink-faint italic">
                            {{ 'calendar.share.day_free'|trans }}
                        </p>
                    {% else %}
                        <ul class="divide-y divide-line">
                            {% for entry in day.entries %}
                                {% include 'sharing/_entry_row.html.twig' with {
                                    entry: entry,
                                    zone: view.zone,
                                    timeFormat: rowTimeFormat,
                                } only %}
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    {% endif %}
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ol>
    {% endif %}

    <footer class="mt-8 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        <a href="{{ icsPath }}"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-field bg-field px-2.5 py-1.5 font-medium text-ink-soft hover:bg-hover transition-colors">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-calendar-plus text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {{ 'calendar.share.subscribe'|trans }}
        </a>

        <span>{{ 'calendar.share.footer'|trans }}</span>
    </footer>
{% endblock %}
